    phy: qcom-usb-hs: apply initialization sequences starting at offset zero
    
    qcom,init-seq lists vendor-register offset/value pairs, and offset zero
    is valid. A zero-address sentinel therefore skips a sequence beginning
    at zero, including the existing MSM8226, MSM8916 and MSM8939 sequences.
    
    Store the number of pairs instead, retain the flexible array with its
    count annotation, and reject a property containing an incomplete pair.
    This causes the existing MSM8916/MSM8939 tuning bytes to take effect;
    those platforms require separate hardware validation.
    
    Refresh Timothy Schmidt's existing flexible-array draft onto the
    verified current PHY-next tree. The original was developed with Claude
    Opus 5.5. Codex (GPT-6) assisted this refresh and actual-source probe,
    power and rollback models. There are 782 cases and 47691 checks,
    including the three pinned SoC sequences, zero offsets in each position,
    empty/absent sequences and malformed lengths before data access.
    All pass with address, undefined-behavior and leak sanitizers; the
    original source and three independent regression controls fail.
    
    Native Qualcomm ARM and ARM64 PHY, generic PHY, ULPI bus and viewport
    objects compile with W=1 without diagnostics. Resource, firmware and
    ULPI services are modeled. No current-tree boot, electrical tuning,
    USB data/OTG behavior or physical MSM8916/MSM8939 acceptance is claimed.
    
    Fixes: e2427b09ba92 ("phy: Add support for Qualcomm's USB HS phy")

